    "diagnosis": "Solid pleuropulmonary blastoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Solid sarcomatous portions of type&nbsp;II and III pleuropulmonary blastomas commonly have spindled, ovoid, and stellate cells in a pale-blue matrix, resembling embryonal rhabdomyosarcoma. These areas are often associated with more tightly packed blastemal nests of cells with hyperchromatic nuclei and high N:C&nbsp;ratio. A small round blastemal nest is seen in the lower-left portion of this photomicrograph.",
    "source": "D. Ashley Hill",
